-- Restores an index unintentionally dropped by the previous migration
-- (20260908105617_add_container_tracking_eta_change_state).
--
-- That migration was generated by `prisma migrate dev` while adding the
-- unrelated Phase B ETA-change-tracking columns to ContainerTracking. Prisma
-- diffs the full schema.prisma against migration history, and at the time it
-- ran, the (pre-existing, uncommitted, unrelated) working copy of
-- schema.prisma no longer declared a unique constraint on
-- StockExit.idempotencyKey — so Prisma bundled a `DROP INDEX
-- "stock_exits_idempotencyKey_key"` into that migration alongside the
-- intended new columns. That index is a real safety mechanism (see
-- 20260828103205_add_stock_exit_idempotency_key's own migration comment): it
-- prevents a duplicate anonymous-walk-in-sale request from double-deducting
-- stock and double-crediting a collector's ledger account. Dropping it was
-- never part of this (Phase B) change and is restored here, unconditionally,
-- rather than left in place or silently folded into the prior migration.
--
-- This does not resolve the underlying drift (schema.prisma's StockExit
-- model still doesn't declare this constraint, so a future `prisma migrate
-- dev` run for an unrelated change could bundle the same accidental drop
-- again) — that belongs to whoever is doing the in-progress StockExit
-- idempotency work already reflected elsewhere in the uncommitted schema
-- changes, not to this migration. Flagged separately in the Phase B report.
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "stock_exits_idempotencyKey_key" ON "stock_exits"("idempotencyKey");
